<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures edge down as supply eases.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures edge down as supply eases.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian wheat futures edged back slightly in continued low-volume trading on Friday.</p>
<p>The near March contract fell by A$2.00 to A$170.00 a tonne in nine lots traded.</p>
<p>Andrew Szonyi of Perth Commodities and Futures Brokers Pty Ltd said Australian wheat supply tightness appeared to have eased slightly, providing breathing space for the market.</p>
<p>Settlement prices for nearer-term futures eased by about A$2.00 a tonne.  </p>
